* Static CMOS gate library (transistor level) used by the Part C test circuit.
* Same transistors, terminals and widths as the Part B gate netlists
* (inv.cir ... or2.cir) and as part_b_gate_level/gatelib/gates.py, which the ML
* side uses; step1_collect_spice.py checks that all three agree.
* Ports: inputs, out, vdd. Body: NMOS at 0, PMOS at vdd. L = 45 nm.
* M<name> drain gate source body model

.subckt INV a out vdd
Mp out a vdd vdd pmos W=180n L=45n
Mn out a 0   0   nmos W=90n  L=45n
.ends INV

* x = node between the series NMOS
.subckt NAND2 a b out vdd
Mpa out a vdd vdd pmos W=180n L=45n
Mpb out b vdd vdd pmos W=180n L=45n
Mna out a x   0   nmos W=180n L=45n
Mnb x   b 0   0   nmos W=180n L=45n
.ends NAND2

* y = node between the series PMOS
.subckt NOR2 a b out vdd
Mpa y   a vdd vdd pmos W=360n L=45n
Mpb out b y   vdd pmos W=360n L=45n
Mna out a 0   0   nmos W=90n  L=45n
Mnb out b 0   0   nmos W=90n  L=45n
.ends NOR2

* AND2 = NAND2 (output n1) + INV
.subckt AND2 a b out vdd
Mnand_pa n1  a  vdd vdd pmos W=180n L=45n
Mnand_pb n1  b  vdd vdd pmos W=180n L=45n
Mnand_na n1  a  x   0   nmos W=180n L=45n
Mnand_nb x   b  0   0   nmos W=180n L=45n
Minv_p   out n1 vdd vdd pmos W=180n L=45n
Minv_n   out n1 0   0   nmos W=90n  L=45n
.ends AND2

* OR2 = NOR2 (output n1) + INV
.subckt OR2 a b out vdd
Mnor_pa  y   a  vdd vdd pmos W=360n L=45n
Mnor_pb  n1  b  y   vdd pmos W=360n L=45n
Mnor_na  n1  a  0   0   nmos W=90n  L=45n
Mnor_nb  n1  b  0   0   nmos W=90n  L=45n
Minv_p   out n1 vdd vdd pmos W=180n L=45n
Minv_n   out n1 0   0   nmos W=90n  L=45n
.ends OR2
